        "content": "### 1. Vector Differential Calculus: Del, Gradient, Divergence & Curl\n\n> 🟢 **The Vector Differential Operator Del ($\\nabla$):**\n> $$\\mathbf{\\nabla = \\hat{i}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x} + \\hat{j}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y} + \\hat{k}\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z}}$$\n\n#### A. Gradient of a Scalar Field ($\\nabla\\phi$) & Directional Derivative:\n- **Gradient:** $\\mathbf{\\nabla\\phi = \\hat{i}\\frac{\\partial\\phi}{\\partial x} + \\hat{j}\\frac{\\partial\\phi}{\\partial y} + \\hat{k}\\frac{\\partial\\phi}{\\partial z}}$ (normal to level surface $\\phi(x,y,z) = c$).\n- **Unit Normal Vector:** $\\mathbf{\\hat{n} = \\frac{\\nabla\\phi}{|\\nabla\\phi|}}$.\n- **Directional Derivative along $\\vec{a}$:** $\\mathbf{\\text{D.D.} = \\nabla\\phi \\cdot \\frac{\\vec{a}}{|\\vec{a}|}}$ (maximum magnitude $= |\\nabla\\phi|$ in direction of $\\nabla\\phi$).\n\n#### B. Divergence ($\\nabla \\cdot \\vec{F}$) & Curl ($\\nabla \\times \\vec{F}$):\n- **Divergence (Scalar):** $\\mathbf{\\text{div}\\,\\vec{F} = \\nabla \\cdot \\vec{F} = \\frac{\\partial F_1}{\\partial x} + \\frac{\\partial F_2}{\\partial y} + \\frac{\\partial F_3}{\\partial z}}$.\n  - **Solenoidal Field:** $\\mathbf{\\nabla \\cdot \\vec{F} = 0}$.\n- **Curl (Vector):** $\\mathbf{\\text{curl}\\,\\vec{F} = \\nabla \\times \\vec{F} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\hat{i} & \\hat{j} & \\hat{k} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z} \\\\ F_1 & F_2 & F_3 \\end{vmatrix}}$.\n  - **Irrotational (Conservative) Field:** $\\mathbf{\\nabla \\times \\vec{F} = \\vec{0} \\iff \\vec{F} = \\nabla\\phi}$.\n\n---\n\n**University Question (6 Marks - MMDU Question Paper):**\nFind the directional derivative of $\\phi = x^2 y z + 4 x z^2$ at point $P(1, -2, -1)$ in the direction of vector $\\vec{a} = 2\\hat{i} - \\hat{j} - 2\\hat{k}$.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 🚀: Calculate $\\nabla\\phi$ at $P(1, -2, -1)$**\n$$\\nabla\\phi = (2xyz + 4z^2)\\hat{i} + (x^2 z)\\hat{j} + (x^2 y + 8xz)\\hat{k} \\Big|_{(1,-2,-1)} = 8\\hat{i} - \\hat{j} - 10\\hat{k}$$\n\n**Step 2 ⚡: Project onto Unit Vector $\\hat{a}$**\n$$\\hat{a} = \\frac{2\\hat{i} - \\hat{j} - 2\\hat{k}}{\\sqrt{4 + 1 + 4}} = \\frac{2\\hat{i} - \\hat{j} - 2\\hat{k}}{3} \\implies \\text{D.D.} = \\nabla\\phi \\cdot \\hat{a} = \\frac{16 + 1 + 20}{3} = \\frac{37}{3}$$\n\n<div class=\"example-answer-box\">\n🎯 Directional Derivative: $\\mathbf{\\frac{37}{3} \\approx 12.33}$.\n</div>\n\n---\n\n**University Question (6 Marks - MMDU Question Paper):**\nProve that $\\vec{F} = (y^2 \\cos x + z^3)\\hat{i} + (2y \\sin x - 4)\\hat{j} + (3x z^2 + 2)\\hat{k}$ is irrotational, and find its scalar potential $\\phi$.\n\n---\n\n**Step 1 🚀: Evaluate $\\text{curl}\\,\\vec{F} = \\nabla \\times \\vec{F}$**\n$$\\nabla \\times \\vec{F} = \\begin{vmatrix} \\hat{i} & \\hat{j} & \\hat{k} \\\\ \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x} & \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y} & \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z} \\\\ y^2 \\cos x + z^3 & 2y \\sin x - 4 & 3xz^2 + 2 \\end{vmatrix} = (0)\\hat{i} - (3z^2 - 3z^2)\\hat{j} + (2y\\cos x - 2y\\cos x)\\hat{k} = \\vec{0}$$\n\n**Step 2 ⚡: Integrate Exact Differential $d\\phi = \\vec{F} \\cdot d\\vec{r}$**\n$$d\\phi = d(y^2 \\sin x) + d(x z^3) - d(4y) + d(2z) \\implies \\phi = y^2 \\sin x + x z^3 - 4y + 2z + C$$\n\n<div class=\"example-answer-box\">\n🎯 $\\nabla \\times \\vec{F} = \\vec{0}$ (Irrotational) | Scalar Potential: $\\mathbf{\\phi = y^2 \\sin x + x z^3 - 4y + 2z + C}$.\n</div>"
